      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`_coerce` in `vllm/parser/chat_parsing/response_parser.py` converts `number`-typed tool arguments with `float()` first, so integers above 2**53 are silently rounded. This PR tries `int()` first, as the `integer` branch already does. #55743 fixed the same problem in `vllm/tool_parsers/utils.py::coerce_to_schema_type`; this is the same fix for the chat-parsing path.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `_coerce(\"9223372036854775807\", (\"number\",))` returns `9223372036854775807` instead of `9223372036854775808`.\n- Decimal, exponent, NaN and infinity inputs (`\"2.5\"`, `\"1e3\"`, `\"5.0\"`, `\"nan\"`, `\"inf\"`) behave as before, because `int()` rejects them and the existing float path runs.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew test `test_coerce_number_keeps_large_integers_exact` in `tests/parser/test_chat_parsing.py`.\n\nBefore the fix:\n\n```\n$ pytest tests/parser/test_chat_parsing.py -k large_integers\nE       AssertionError: 9223372036854775808 != 9223372036854775807\nFAILED tests/parser/test_chat_parsing.py::ToolArgCoercionTest::test_coerce_number_keeps_large_integers_exact\n1 failed, 76 deselected\n```\n\nAfter the fix:\n\n```\n$ pytest tests/parser/test_chat_parsing.py\n77 passed, 384 subtests passed\n```\n\n`pre-commit run --files <changed files>` passes (ruff check/format, mypy, typos).\n\nEnvironment: CPU only (ARM Neoverse-N1, 4 cores), Python 3.12, torch 2.14.0. No GPU or model run; the change is limited to argument type coercion.\n\n## Details\n\nThe `number` branch did `number = float(raw)` and then `int(number)` for whole numbers, so the integer was rounded to the nearest double before conversion. Trying `int(raw)` first keeps the exact value for integer literals and leaves every other input on the old path.\n\nDuplicate check: #61410 also edits `_coerce`, but only the `integer` branch (whole-number floats such as `\"...807.0\"`); it does not touch the `number` branch. No other open PR touches `vllm/parser/chat_parsing/`.\n\nAI assistance was used to help find the issue and draft the change; I reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
